      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Sunny. Same as my reply on Discord:\n\nI agree adapters need to be distinguishable in inventory. A type enum on this interface may not be needed for that, though: the information is already defined elsewhere (Decorator.Asset for the product, Connector.Port.PortProtocol for the protocol), and a single type for the whole adapter would be inaccurate when one adapter runs more than one protocol.\n\n    adapter object\n      interfaces on this object:\n        Item.NetworkAdapter  \u003d\u003e it is a network adapter     (89247, this change under review)\n        Decorator.Asset      \u003d\u003e Manufacturer, Model, PartNumber, SKU (which product)\n\n      linked by the \"connecting\" association:\n        |-- port 0 object\n        |     Connector.Port \u003d\u003e PortProtocol \u003d Ethernet     (89248, under review)\n        `-- port 1 object\n              Connector.Port \u003d\u003e PortProtocol \u003d InfiniBand   (95051, under review)\n                                (what each port runs)\n\nIf my understanding is incorrect, please feel free to correct me. Thanks!",
